      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "YES YOSHI (3) clearly looks the one to beat off a fourth at Bendigo in BM78 grade first up, beaten a length and a half as a well-supported favourite after jumping awkwardly. He drops to a BM66, has proven form at 1200m and Damian Lane going on adds further confidence. Should go close. KING WEST (4) is the obvious danger on consistency, having been beaten a head at each of his past two BM62 runs and bringing a strong record at this track and distance, should be right there. HUSTLE IN HEELS (7) won first-up at Cranbourne, beating Holding Captive by a neck as favourite. Can go on with it. SIRIUSLY BRIGHT (8) is another last-start winner, coming off a Kilmore BM56 success. Harder now but in the mix. CARDI BEE (5) has the ability to run well fresh.",
